Running `gnatpolyglot  --help`
================================================================================

Usage: gnatpolyglot [-hqv] [--version] [--header-file=<headerFile>] [COMMAND]
GNATpolyglot - Multi-language interface generator.
See documentation for more information.
  -h, --help      display usage and exit
      --header-file=<headerFile>
                  prepend the content of the given file to all sources
                    generated by GNATpolyglot.
  -q              be quiet
  -v              verbose output
      --version   display version and exit
Commands:
  validator   Validate a json proxy
  ada2proxy   Create a proxy for the given Ada project.
  proxy2cpp   Create the C++ interface of a proxy representation
  proxy2java  Create the Java interface of a proxy representation
  proxy2rust  Create the Rust interface of a proxy representation
  setup       Set up the GNATpolyglot runtime.


Running `gnatpolyglot setup --help`
================================================================================

Usage: gnatpolyglot setup [-hqv] [--check-only] [--target-only]
                          [--from-lang=<fromLang>] [--header-file=<headerFile>]
                          --prefix=<prefixPath> [--to-lang=<toLang>]
Set up the GNATpolyglot runtime.
If none of --from-lang or --to-lang is passed, then the entire runtime is
created.
If only --from-lang is set, only the runtime used to build the bindings for
that language is created.
If --from-lang and --to-lang are both set, both the runtime for building the
bindings and the interfaces are created, unless --target-only is set in which
case only the runtime for the interfaces is created.
Note that --to-lang cannot be used without --from-lang.
      --prefix=<prefixPath>
                           installation path
      --check-only         do not copy the runtime. Instead, emit warnings if
                             the runtime was modified.
  -h, --help               display sub-command usage and exit
      --from-lang=<fromLang>
                           input language
      --to-lang=<toLang>   output language
      --target-only        only create the runtime for the target
      --header-file=<headerFile>
                           prepend the content of the given file to all sources
                             generated by GNATpolyglot.
  -q                       be quiet
  -v                       verbose output


